WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:04.480
With so many new Netflix originals hitting
the service in August, you'll have more to

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:06.700
watch than ever in the coming month.

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:11.459
From wild new series to new stand-up specials
to a laundry list of original films, there's

00:00:11.459 --> 00:00:13.129
a lot to look forward to.

00:00:13.129 --> 00:00:17.040
Let's take a look at what's arriving and what's
worth getting excited about, starting with

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.260
the Netflix originals.

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:20.550
Switched

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:25.350
August is kicking off with Switched, a suspenseful
Japanese drama about a high school girl whose

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:27.310
life gets stolen by another student.

00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:31.490
And not just her life, her rival snatches
her physical body, leaving her fighting to

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:33.730
restore everything to the way it was.

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:36.010
Take a look when Switched premieres on August
1st.

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:38.410
I Am a Killer

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:42.780
True crime is blowing up all over Netflix,
and the latest piece of fallout is the upcoming

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:44.380
series I Am a Killer.

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:48.730
In this show, the cameras are going into death
row for interviews with convicted murderers.

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:49.950
Some are remorseful.

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:51.550
Others...a little less so.

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:55.010
"I don't feel bad about it.

00:00:55.010 --> 00:00:56.750
Hah hah hah."

00:00:56.750 --> 00:01:01.130
Take the dive into darkness when I Am a Killer
drops on August 3rd.

00:01:01.130 --> 00:01:02.760
Long Live Brij Mohan

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:07.010
Stuck in a loveless marriage and struggling
under a mountain of debt, Brij Mohan doesn't

00:01:07.010 --> 00:01:08.500
have a whole lot going for him.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:12.430
So he takes the only way out he can think
of, he fakes his own death and restarts his

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:13.830
life with a new identity.

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:17.780
But he can't run forever, and it isn't long
before his past catches up with him.

00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:20.310
Take a look when it arrives on August 3rd.

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:21.700
Cocaine Coast

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:26.520
In this Netflix series, a poor fisherman sets
out to live the dream by shuttling drugs between

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:30.450
Spain and Latin America, getting filthy rich
in the process.

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:35.100
It's a story that's been told plenty of times
before, but Cocaine Coast looks like it has

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:37.120
enough charm to pull it off at least one more
time.

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:39.420
Check it out on August 3rd.

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:40.420
Like Father

00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:44.530
This Netflix film sees Kristen Bell starring
as an altar-dumped bride who heads out on

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:46.979
a cruise to do a little soul searching.

00:01:46.979 --> 00:01:50.979
What she doesn't remember is getting black-out
drunk with her estranged dad after the wedding

00:01:50.979 --> 00:01:53.580
disaster and inviting him onto the cruise
with her.

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:56.820
"Somehow I dragged him onto this cruise that
was supposed to be my honeymoon."

00:01:56.820 --> 00:02:01.060
Now, they're stuck on a ship with nowhere
to run except into their tangled emotions.

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:03.080
It's just too bad they hate each other.

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:06.560
Like Father sails onto Netflix on August 3rd.

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:07.579
Marching Orders

00:02:07.579 --> 00:02:11.190
You've sweated right through the dramas of
Last Chance U; you've witnessed the ups and

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:15.700
downs of Friday Night Tykes and cheered a
young team into greatness with Coach Snoop.

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:19.480
Now get ready for a brand new emotional journey
with Marching Orders.

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:23.090
When the players leave the field, the marching
band take center stage.

00:02:23.090 --> 00:02:27.431
Marching Orders follows the Marching Wildcats
of Bethune-Cookman University, one of the

00:02:27.431 --> 00:02:29.700
country's biggest college bands.

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:32.360
Marching Orders takes the field on August
3rd.

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:33.400
Mr. Sunshine

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:38.700
This emotional series made its Netflix premiere
in early July 2018, but hasn't made much of

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:41.150
a splash with Western audiences quite yet.

00:02:41.150 --> 00:02:45.720
The historical drama follows a Korean soldier
who lives in the U.S. for years before returning

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:49.819
to South Korea and falling in love with the
daughter of a high-class aristocrat.

00:02:49.819 --> 00:02:54.030
With both drama and thrills, it's no wonder
that Mr. Sunshine has been gaining popularity

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:55.030
in Korea.

00:02:55.030 --> 00:02:59.670
August will see a new episode land on Netflix
every Saturday, starting on the 4th.

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:01.180
On Children

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:05.300
With its strong Black Mirror vibes, On Children
looks like an intriguing new show.

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:09.930
The trailer is full of technological terror,
parallel universes, and memory swapping, and

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:13.519
we honestly can't tell what's going on half
the time, but it seems like a lot of fun.

00:03:13.519 --> 00:03:16.879
Give it a shot when On Children drops on August
4th.

00:03:16.879 --> 00:03:18.940
72 Dangerous Animals: Asia

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:25.590
Netflix's 72 Dangerous Animals series takes
an admittedly goofy approach to nature commentary.

00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:32.950
"A villain with a killer sting, but one that
can also use its powers for good."

00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:37.270
The idea is, each episode picks a handful
of similar dangerous critters, runs through

00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:40.550
their strengths and weaknesses, and then ranks
them in order of danger.

00:03:40.550 --> 00:03:44.580
"Part the flames to make way for the FIRE
ANT."

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:48.909
The newest entry in the series is set to explore
the rich world of Asia, and all the creepy

00:03:48.909 --> 00:03:50.260
crawlies who live there.

00:03:50.260 --> 00:03:52.549
Look for it on August 10th.

00:03:52.549 --> 00:03:54.099
The House of Flowers

00:03:54.099 --> 00:03:59.460
Equal parts telenovela and Six Feet Under-style
dysfunctional family comedy, La Casa de las

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:03.040
Flores, or "The House of Flowers," follows
a family that owns a flower shop.

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:07.430
Even though they all look perfect on the outside,
each one of them has a dark secret just waiting

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:08.440
to come to light.

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:12.799
When the father's mistress hangs herself at
the family store, it opens the floodgates,

00:04:12.799 --> 00:04:15.190
sending all those secrets flooding into the
open.

00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:20.529
It definitely looks like a fun, darkly comedic
ride, and you can check it out on August 10th.

00:04:20.529 --> 00:04:21.849
Million Pound Menu

00:04:21.849 --> 00:04:26.339
Yet another collaboration between Netflix
and the BBC, Million Pound Menu is sort of

00:04:26.339 --> 00:04:30.599
like a spin on Shark Tank where all the hopeful
entrepreneurs are going into the restaurant

00:04:30.599 --> 00:04:31.599
business.

00:04:31.599 --> 00:04:35.719
It's high stakes, flame-broiled fun, and the
whole first season hits the pan on August

00:04:35.719 --> 00:04:36.719
10th.

00:04:36.719 --> 00:04:37.719
Zion

00:04:37.719 --> 00:04:42.319
This heartwarming documentary follows Zion
Clark, a wrestler at Kent State University

00:04:42.319 --> 00:04:43.860
who was born without legs.

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:48.550
But Clark's motto is "no excuses," so he's
made it his life's goal to not let anything

00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:49.550
hold him back.

00:04:49.550 --> 00:04:54.000
With Zion, Netflix is taking a long, intimate
look at Clark's life and the inspired optimism

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:56.690
that drives him to continue to excel as a
wrestler.

00:04:56.690 --> 00:04:59.619
Tune in for the emotional journey on August
10th.

00:04:59.619 --> 00:05:01.569
Insatiable: Season 1

00:05:01.569 --> 00:05:04.889
After getting picked on her whole life for
being overweight, Patty gets the chance to

00:05:04.889 --> 00:05:07.939
get back at her bullies after spending a summer
slimming down.

00:05:07.939 --> 00:05:12.249
That's the premise of Insatiable, a dark revenge
comedy that's already garnered some online

00:05:12.249 --> 00:05:13.399
controversy.

00:05:13.399 --> 00:05:17.789
Based on the trailer, Insatiable looks like
a violent, comedic tale where anything goes

00:05:17.789 --> 00:05:20.089
and the normal rules of the world don't apply.

00:05:20.089 --> 00:05:22.169
Take a look when it lands on August 10th.

00:05:22.169 --> 00:05:23.819
All About the Washingtons

00:05:23.819 --> 00:05:29.449
Fans of the hip hop group Run-DMC are no doubt
familiar with Reverend Run, aka Joseph Simmons,

00:05:29.449 --> 00:05:31.889
who's also an on-again-off-again reality star.

00:05:31.889 --> 00:05:35.960
It looks like 2018 will be another on-again
year for the Rev, because he's coming back

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:39.149
to the small screen with the sitcom All About
the Washingtons.

00:05:39.149 --> 00:05:43.219
Simmons stars as Joey, an ex-rapper who's
easing into retirement, giving his wife a

00:05:43.219 --> 00:05:46.070
chance to be the entrepreneur she always dreamed
of being.

00:05:46.070 --> 00:05:49.469
Along the way, they'll have to figure out
how to keep their wild family in check.

00:05:49.469 --> 00:05:51.340
Look for it on August 10th.

00:05:51.340 --> 00:05:52.340
The Package

00:05:52.340 --> 00:05:56.650
If we're being completely honest, Netflix's
comedies can be really hit or miss.

00:05:56.650 --> 00:06:00.189
For every one that's actually funny, you're
bound to come across five that just leave

00:06:00.189 --> 00:06:01.280
you groaning.

00:06:01.280 --> 00:06:02.719
Which one will The Package be?

00:06:02.719 --> 00:06:04.699
All indications point toward the former.

00:06:04.699 --> 00:06:08.729
The dark comedy sees a gang of teens heading
out into the woods for spring break, only

00:06:08.729 --> 00:06:10.629
for things to go horribly wrong.

00:06:10.629 --> 00:06:12.780
Tune in for all the hijinks on August 10th.

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:16.569
The Guernsey Literary and Potato Peel Pie
Society

00:06:16.569 --> 00:06:20.569
Based on the book of the same name, this mouthful
of a movie is about a writer who decides to

00:06:20.569 --> 00:06:24.249
pen a book about a literary club that formed
during World War II.

00:06:24.249 --> 00:06:28.080
While she's researching her novel, she gets
caught up in the story of the young men who

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:32.240
survived the occupation of the Guernsey islands,
falling in love with one of them.

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:36.710
If the Netflix film is anything like the book,
you can look forward to a whirlwind historical

00:06:36.710 --> 00:06:39.839
romance about the power of courage and loyalty.

00:06:39.839 --> 00:06:42.860
Find out when it premieres on Netflix on August
10th.

00:06:42.860 --> 00:06:43.909
Magic for Humans

00:06:43.909 --> 00:06:48.360
Caught somewhere between a magic act, reality
show, and comedy series, Magic for Humans

00:06:48.360 --> 00:06:52.770
sees magician Justin Willman traveling around
performing illusions and telling jokes in

00:06:52.770 --> 00:06:54.270
a new spin on street magic.

00:06:54.270 --> 00:06:58.229
It sounds like a great time, and it premieres
on August 17th.

00:06:58.229 --> 00:06:59.349
Stay Here

00:06:59.349 --> 00:07:03.649
From cooking shows to travelogues, Netflix
has been flooding their service with great

00:07:03.649 --> 00:07:05.039
reality programming.

00:07:05.039 --> 00:07:09.660
On August 17th, they're adding to that lineup
with Stay Here, a property fixer-upper reality

00:07:09.660 --> 00:07:14.509
show that sees an interior designer working
with homeowners to spruce up their rental

00:07:14.509 --> 00:07:15.610
properties.

00:07:15.610 --> 00:07:17.330
The Motive

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:22.169
Every writer needs inspiration, and in The
Motive, it comes from some pretty dark places.

00:07:22.169 --> 00:07:27.089
The movie focuses on Alvaro, a wannabe writer
who moves into a new apartment after a divorce.

00:07:27.089 --> 00:07:31.310
There, he begins manipulating his neighbors
to use them as inspiration for the characters

00:07:31.310 --> 00:07:32.310
in his book.

00:07:32.310 --> 00:07:35.270
As you might expect, things get out of control
pretty fast.

00:07:35.270 --> 00:07:39.479
Part comedy and part thriller, The Motive
arrives on August 17th.

00:07:39.479 --> 00:07:40.939
Ultraviolet

00:07:40.939 --> 00:07:45.710
This Polish drama centers on Ola, a woman
who watches a bizarre accident unfold.

00:07:45.710 --> 00:07:49.889
Unable to accept the police's verdict that
the accident was a suicide, Ola begins to

00:07:49.889 --> 00:07:55.210
dig into it on her own, leading her to stumble
across a secret online community called Ultraviolet,

00:07:55.210 --> 00:07:59.029
a group of internet vigilantes who tackle
the cases the police can't solve.

00:07:59.029 --> 00:08:02.340
Tune in for all the twists and turns on August
17th.

00:08:02.340 --> 00:08:04.349
Disenchantment: Season 1

00:08:04.349 --> 00:08:08.180
By the time the first teaser for Disenchantment
dropped, the internet was already buzzing

00:08:08.180 --> 00:08:09.180
about the show.

00:08:09.180 --> 00:08:13.949
From Matt Groening, creator of The Simpsons
and Futurama, Disenchantment is set in a fantasy

00:08:13.949 --> 00:08:18.279
world and promises all the same humor fans
of Groening's other shows have come to love.

00:08:18.279 --> 00:08:19.689
"Whew, I'm a good butcher."

00:08:19.689 --> 00:08:22.539
"This is a pet shop."

00:08:22.539 --> 00:08:27.270
Take a look when the first 10 episodes of
Disenchantment land on August 17th.

00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:29.369
To All the Boys I've Loved Before

00:08:29.369 --> 00:08:33.610
This teen drama follows Lara Jean, a high
school girl who has an unfortunate habit of

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:36.560
writing long, secret love letters to all her
crushes.

00:08:36.560 --> 00:08:40.169
It's unfortunate because out of nowhere, all
those letters end up getting mailed out to

00:08:40.169 --> 00:08:45.270
the boys in question, turning Lara's high
school life into a circus of unexpected attention.

00:08:45.270 --> 00:08:49.339
The upcoming movie is based on the popular
book of the same name, and drops on August

00:08:49.339 --> 00:08:50.639
17th.

00:08:50.639 --> 00:08:54.400
The Investigator: A British Crime Story: Season
2

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:58.759
Netflix's popular true crime offerings like
Making a Murderer, The Staircase, and Evil

00:08:58.759 --> 00:09:03.410
Genius tend to get all the attention, but
the real crime is how overlooked some of their

00:09:03.410 --> 00:09:04.459
other series are.

00:09:04.459 --> 00:09:06.650
Case in point: The Investigator.

00:09:06.650 --> 00:09:10.709
This British true crime series dives into
some of the most enduring mysteries of the

00:09:10.709 --> 00:09:11.709
UK.

00:09:11.709 --> 00:09:15.600
With the second season, the show is honing
its focus on two serial killers and their

00:09:15.600 --> 00:09:18.779
possible connection to a rash of unsolved
murders.

00:09:18.779 --> 00:09:21.300
Take a look on August 19th.

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:22.300
Deadwind

00:09:22.300 --> 00:09:27.390
After this series swept Finland and became
something of an overnight sensation, Netflix

00:09:27.390 --> 00:09:31.509
swooped in to grab the international distribution
rights, like they often do.

00:09:31.509 --> 00:09:33.620
In this case, it looks like a great decision.

00:09:33.620 --> 00:09:37.910
The series follows a grieving detective who
gets caught up in a murder investigation just

00:09:37.910 --> 00:09:42.129
two months after the death of her husband,
leading her down a spiraling path of violence

00:09:42.129 --> 00:09:43.129
and grief.

00:09:43.129 --> 00:09:47.080
For anyone looking for a dark, suspenseful
show to get caught up in, Deadwind looks like

00:09:47.080 --> 00:09:48.290
it's just the ticket.

00:09:48.290 --> 00:09:50.550
Tune in on August 23rd.

00:09:50.550 --> 00:09:52.019
The After Party

00:09:52.019 --> 00:09:55.010
Get ready for a musical roller coaster with
The After Party.

00:09:55.010 --> 00:09:59.730
California rapper Kyle Harvey stars in this
hip hop-infused comedy about a rapper on the

00:09:59.730 --> 00:10:02.709
outs with his fans who gets one final chance
at redemption.

00:10:02.709 --> 00:10:06.950
Check out The After Party when it drops on
Netflix on August 24th.

00:10:06.950 --> 00:10:09.320
The Innocents: Season 1

00:10:09.320 --> 00:10:12.540
Netflix has been dropping teasers for The
Innocents for months now, but none of those

00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:16.139
trailers have revealed a whole lot about the
series' actual story.

00:10:16.139 --> 00:10:20.149
Apart from some hints of a bizarre plot involving
a girl who turns into someone else, we really

00:10:20.149 --> 00:10:21.149
have no idea what to expect.

00:10:21.149 --> 00:10:22.910
"Look, it's me.

00:10:22.910 --> 00:10:27.589
Harry, it's me."

00:10:27.589 --> 00:10:33.209
Regardless, The Innocents looks like a seriously
twisted show, with amazing production design

00:10:33.209 --> 00:10:35.029
and a fantastic cast.

00:10:35.029 --> 00:10:36.939
Take a look on August 24th.

00:10:36.939 --> 00:10:37.939
Ghoul

00:10:37.939 --> 00:10:42.640
It's been awhile since a good new horror series
showed up on Netflix, and it looks like Ghoul

00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:44.279
is set to break the dry spell.

00:10:44.279 --> 00:10:48.339
The show is set in a secret government center,
where one of the prisoners may be a little

00:10:48.339 --> 00:10:49.850
more demon than human.

00:10:49.850 --> 00:10:54.089
Blumhouse, the company behind movies like
Get Out and The Purge, is producing the three-part

00:10:54.089 --> 00:10:57.940
horror extravaganza, which lands on August
24th.

00:10:57.940 --> 00:10:59.889
Ozark: Season 2

00:10:59.889 --> 00:11:04.120
It's been a long, bitter wait, but fans of
Ozark can finally see a glimmer of hope on

00:11:04.120 --> 00:11:05.120
the horizon.

00:11:05.120 --> 00:11:09.610
The show, which stars Jason Bateman as a financial
advisor caught up in the underworld of drug

00:11:09.610 --> 00:11:14.480
trafficking, was nominated for a Golden Globe
and quickly built a legion of dedicated fans.

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:19.430
It's both dark and humorous, violent and surprisingly
heartfelt, and we're all hoping for more of

00:11:19.430 --> 00:11:23.620
the same when Season 2 floats onto Netflix
on August 31st.

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:25.949
The Laws of Thermodynamics

00:11:25.949 --> 00:11:30.850
Written and directed by Spanish filmmaker
Mateo Gil, The Laws of Thermodynamics is your

00:11:30.850 --> 00:11:34.129
typical boy-meets-girl scenario, but with
a science twist.

00:11:34.129 --> 00:11:39.510
The core romantic story is wrapped up in theories
about how scientific laws also affect relationships

00:11:39.510 --> 00:11:41.100
and emotions.

00:11:41.100 --> 00:11:44.509
It's a strange genre crossover, sure, but
one that looks like a decidedly interesting

00:11:44.509 --> 00:11:45.949
viewing experience.

00:11:45.949 --> 00:11:48.290
Look for it on August 31.

00:11:48.290 --> 00:11:51.160
Ultimate Beastmaster: Survival of the Fittest

00:11:51.160 --> 00:11:55.149
Strap on your sweatbands and settle in for
the ride as Ultimate Beastmaster: Survival

00:11:55.149 --> 00:11:57.779
of the Fittest leaps onto your streaming queue.

00:11:57.779 --> 00:12:01.970
The fit-and-fun competition will see a whole
new lineup of contestants facing some of the

00:12:01.970 --> 00:12:06.930
most challenging obstacles to date, with plenty
of dramatic commentary to keep it exciting.

00:12:06.930 --> 00:12:10.829
"It's like a Transformer and Godzilla had
a baby or something."

00:12:10.829 --> 00:12:13.749
You can catch all the new episodes on August
31st.

00:12:13.749 --> 00:12:15.879
New standup comedy

00:12:15.879 --> 00:12:20.060
Keep your eyes open for a handful of brand
new comedy releases hitting Netflix throughout

00:12:20.060 --> 00:12:21.060
the month.

00:12:21.060 --> 00:12:25.519
On August 10th, Demetri Martin takes the stage
with The Overthinker, riffing on topics ranging

00:12:25.519 --> 00:12:29.379
from road rage to horoscopes to being the
kind of guy who overthinks everything.

00:12:29.379 --> 00:12:35.339
Then, on August 24th, look for Bert Kreischer:
Secret Time, followed by Part 2 of Netflix's

00:12:35.339 --> 00:12:39.660
recent comedy series The Comedy Lineup, which
sees multiple comics taking the stage for

00:12:39.660 --> 00:12:41.439
short 15-minute sets.

00:12:41.439 --> 00:12:43.560
You'll be able to stream that on August 31st.

00:12:43.560 --> 00:12:46.420
That's all the Netflix originals arriving
in August.

00:12:46.420 --> 00:12:51.069
Now let's take a look at all the other movies
and TV shows hitting the streaming service.

00:12:51.069 --> 00:12:52.519
New movies

00:12:52.519 --> 00:12:56.209
The best part of each month's Netflix lineup
is invariably the addition of a brand new

00:12:56.209 --> 00:13:00.040
slew of old favorites, and August is bringing
plenty of classics.

00:13:00.040 --> 00:13:06.329
On the action front, look for films like Batman
Begins, Constantine, and 1985 Western Silverado,

00:13:06.329 --> 00:13:08.589
all of which show up on the first.

00:13:08.589 --> 00:13:13.899
"You can't do this."

00:13:13.899 --> 00:13:15.220
"Really?"

00:13:15.220 --> 00:13:22.769
There are also plenty of laughs to look forward
to this August, with classics like Steel Magnolias,

00:13:22.769 --> 00:13:26.300
Clerks, and Stripes shouldering their way
onto Netflix on the first.

00:13:26.300 --> 00:13:30.339
"Razzle dazzle, hut two three four."

00:13:30.339 --> 00:13:35.220
On the 16th, you can sit back and watch Steve
Carell build a biblical boat in Evan Almighty,

00:13:35.220 --> 00:13:39.860
and on the 21st, witness Jack Black's and
Michael Cera's epic journey across prehistory

00:13:39.860 --> 00:13:41.910
with the slapstick comedy Year One.

00:13:41.910 --> 00:13:45.519
"Hey guys, I'm trying to enjoy the sacrifice
with my family.

00:13:45.519 --> 00:13:46.519
Do you mind?"

00:13:46.519 --> 00:13:49.449
Chances are none of those will tickle your
terror bone, but don't worry.

00:13:49.449 --> 00:13:54.290
August is also bringing Dreamcatcher, which
you can catch on the first along with Chernobyl

00:13:54.290 --> 00:13:58.620
Diaries, about some mutant tomfoolery at the
Chernobyl nuclear plant.

00:13:58.620 --> 00:14:02.890
Finally, follow that up with the 2015 horror
film Emelie on the second.

00:14:02.890 --> 00:14:04.269
What's not to love?

00:14:04.269 --> 00:14:05.499
New television

00:14:05.499 --> 00:14:08.509
It'll be a good month for bingeing your favorite
shows this August.

00:14:08.509 --> 00:14:13.189
Highlights for this month include Season 5
of The Originals on August 9th, Season 5 of

00:14:13.189 --> 00:14:18.209
The 100 on August 15th, and Season 5 of Young
&amp; Hungry on August 24th.

00:14:18.209 --> 00:14:21.639
Fans of the heavenly comedy The Good Place
will also have a reason to look forward to

00:14:21.639 --> 00:14:26.009
August, which sees the arrival of the second
season of the Emmy-nominated show.

00:14:26.009 --> 00:14:29.410
When she's accidentally sent to "the Good
Place," Eleanor decides that there's never

00:14:29.410 --> 00:14:33.380
been a better time to try to be a good person
and actually earn her spot there.

00:14:33.380 --> 00:14:35.689
Look for the second season on August 28th.

